Final Plat/UDC-15-00425
1
STAFF REPORT - SUMMATION

Saddle Ridge, 7th Filing
Final Plat Process

CASE NUMBER(s):
UDC-15-00425

SUBDIVISION CODE: SDRA

PREPARED BY:
Josh Tetzlaff

MEETING DATES:       August 3, 2015 – Planning Commission
August 24, 2015 – City Council

REQUIRED DOCUMENTS SUBMISSION: The following required documents have been submitted and
reviewed by staff.
●
Complete Application
●
Final Plat Map
●
Drainage Worksheet
●
Traffic Impact Study
●
Environmental Impact Assessment

RECOMMENDATION: The Development Department recommends approval of the Final Plat pursuant to
Section 2.1.3.d of the Cheyenne Unified Development Code (UDC), with the following three (3)
conditions:
1) The words “subdivision” and “City of” are removed from the title block;
2) The donation statements are updated to donate the land to the City of Cheyenne, not the Parks
and Recreation Department; and
3) Complete an agreement with WyDOT concerning future cost sharing when traffic control
improvements at US Highway 30 and Whitney Road are warranted.

PLANNING COMMISSION UPDATE: At its regular meeting on August 3, 2015, the Planning
Commission voted to approve the Final Plat for Saddle Ridge, 7th Filing with the following two (2)
conditions:
1) The words “subdivision” and “City of” are removed from the title block; and
2) The donation statements are updated to donate the land to the City of Cheyenne, not the Parks
and Recreation Department.

The Planning Commission opted not to include the third condition because it did not believe it should hold
developers to making agreements with third parties.

CITY COUNCIL RECOMMENDATION: The Development Department recommends approval of the
Final Plat, with the following two (2) conditions:
1) The words “subdivision” and “City of” are removed from the title block;
2) The donation statements are updated to donate the land to the City of Cheyenne, not the Parks
and Recreation Department; and
3) Complete an agreement with WyDOT concerning future cost sharing when traffic control
improvements at US Highway 30 and Whitney Road are warranted.
